    鹰 | yīng | falcon; eagle; hawk

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 反应 describes passive or instinctive chemical, physiological, or perceptual reactions provoked by an external stimulus.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 反应 vs. 反映 | fǎnyìng | 反应 means physiological or chemical reaction to an external stimulus (毫无反应), whereas 反映 means reflecting light/images or reporting situations upward to superiors (反映情况).
    2 | 反应 vs. 回应 | huíyìng | 反应 can be involuntary physiological reflex (pupils dilating, chemical fizzing), while 回应 is always an intentional, conscious verbal reply or statement.
    3 | 反应 vs. 态度 | tàidù | 反应 describes immediate behavioral feedback, while 态度 is one's persistent moral stance or emotional disposition toward people and matters.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 面对突如其来的变故与风浪，一个人的第一反应往往最能映射出其内心的修养与定力。慌乱与暴躁只会加剧局势的失控，而沉着冷静地审视现实，才能在瞬息万变的危机中做出最精准、最理智的应对。 | Miànduì tūrúqílái de biàngù yǔ fēnglàng, yí gè rén de dì-yī fǎnyìng wǎngwǎng zuì néng yìngshè chū qí nèixīn de xiūyǎng yǔ dìnglì. Huāngluàn yǔ bàozào zhǐ huì jiājù júshì de shīkòng, ér chénzhuó lěngjìng de shěnshì xiànshí, cáinéng zài shùnxī-wànbiàn de wēijī zhōng zuòchū zuì jīngzhǔn, zuì lǐzhì de yìngduì. | Facing unexpected upheavals, a person's first reaction best mirrors their inner poise. Panic and irritability merely escalate chaos, whereas surveying reality calmly empowers accurate, rational responses in volatile crises. | Ante los giros imprevistos del destino, la primera reacción de una persona retrata la templanza de su ánimo. El desasosiego solo precipita el descontrol, mientras que serenar el juicio permite calibrar una respuesta certera y prudente en la turbulencia.
  #2 | 在复杂的现代宏观经济调控中，政策出台与市场实际反应之间往往存在一定的滞后效应。决策部门必须通过高频动态监测与大数据模型，精准评估市场各微观主体的敏感度，从而确保调控措施达到预期实效。 | Zài fùzá de xiàndài hóngguān jīngjì tiáokòng zhōng, zhèngcè chūtái yǔ shìchǎng shíjì fǎnyìng zhījiān wǎngwǎng cúnzài yídìng de zhìhòu xiàoyìng. Juécè bùmén bìxū tōngguò gāopín dòngtài jiāncè yǔ dàshùjù móxíng, jīngzhǔn pínggū shìchǎng gè wēiguān zhǔtǐ de mǐngǎndù, cóng'ér quèbǎo tiáokòng cuòshī dádào yùqī shíxiào. | In modern macroeconomic management, lags exist between policy rollouts and actual market reactions. Policymakers must employ high-frequency monitoring and big-data models to gauge micro-entity sensitivity, ensuring targeted efficacy. | En la política macroeconómica contemporánea, media un inevitable desfase entre la promulgación de medidas y la reacción del mercado. Las autoridades han de valerse de modelos masivos de datos para calibrar la sensibilidad de los agentes y afinar su eficacia.
